    "id": "old-spec/rev18-05",
    "question": "<p>(i) The complex number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w\"></span> is given by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"w = \\frac{p - 4\\mathrm{i}}{2 - 3\\mathrm{i}}\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> is a real constant.</p><p>(a) Express <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a + bi\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are real constants. Give your answer in its simplest form in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\arg w = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\"></span></p><p>(b) find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(ii) The complex number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span> is given by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"z = (1 - \\lambda\\mathrm{i})(4 + 3\\mathrm{i})\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda\"></span> is a real constant.</p><p>Given that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"|z| = 45\"></div><p>find the possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda\"></span>.</p><p>Give your answers as exact values in their simplest form.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>Multiplying by the conjugate makes the denominator <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2^2+3^2=13\"></span>. An argument of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi/4\"></span> requires equal real and imaginary parts and a positive real part. In the independent modulus condition use the product of the moduli to avoid expanding <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(i)(a) Multiply numerator and denominator by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2+3i\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>The result is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w=[2p+12+(3p-8)i]/13\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) For argument <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pi/4\"></span> the real and imaginary parts are equal and positive. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2p+12=3p-8\"></span>, giving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=20\"></span>, which satisfies positivity. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(ii) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|z|=|1-\\lambda i||4+3i|=5\\sqrt{1+\\lambda^2}=45\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda^2=80\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=\\pm4\\sqrt5\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 8 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev18-05-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for 2017 FP1 · Q4, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev18-06",
    "question": "<p>Given that 4 and 2i-3 are roots of the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^{3}+a x^{2}+b x-52=0\"></span> where a and b are real constants,</p><p>(a) write down the third root of the equation,</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>(b) find the value of a and the value of b.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>The conjugate quadratic is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x+3)^2+4\"></span>, so its constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"13\"></span> is the square of the modulus of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-3+2i\"></span>. Multiplying it by the remaining factor <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x-4\"></span> must give constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-52\"></span>, an immediate check before matching the other coefficients.</p>",
      "<p>(a) The conjugate root is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-3-2i\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) The pair gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x+3)^2+4=x^2+6x+13\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Multiply by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x-4\"></span> to get <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3+2x^2-11x-52\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Comparing coefficients gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=2,\\ b=-11\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 6 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev18-06-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for 2017 FP1 · Q6, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev18-08",
    "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=2 z^{3}-4 z^{2}+15 z-13\"></div><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)\\equiv(z-1)(2 z^{2}+a z+b),\"></span> where a and b are real constants,</p><p>(a) find the value of a and the value of b.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(b) Hence use algebra to find the three roots of the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{f}(z)=0\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>Compare constants first, because only one product contributes to the constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-13\"></span>. Once the known root is removed, complete the square or use the quadratic formula on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2z^2-2z+13\"></span>. Its negative discriminant accounts for the conjugate pair.</p>",
      "<p>(a) Expand the given product. The <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z^2\"></span> and constant coefficients give <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a-2=-4,\\ -b=-13\"></span>, hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=-2,\\ b=13\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) The linear factor gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=1\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>For the other roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=[2\\pm\\sqrt{4-104}]/4\"></span>, <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=(1\\pm5i)/2\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 6 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev18-08-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for 2018 FP1 · Q1, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev18-09",
    "question": "<p>(i) Given that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\frac{3w+7}{5}=\\frac{p-4\\mathrm{i}}{3-\\mathrm{i}}\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> is a real constant</p><p>(a) express <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a+bi\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are real constants.</p><p>Give your answer in its simplest form in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\arg w=-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\"></span></p><p>(b) find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>(ii) Given that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"(z+1-2\\mathrm{i})^{*}=4\\mathrm{i}z\"></div><p>find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=x+iy\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> are real constants.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>In the first quotient the denominator becomes <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3^2+1^2=10\"></span>, so both components are scaled equally. For a point on the negative imaginary axis set its real coordinate to zero and verify its imaginary coordinate is negative. In the separate equation conjugation changes <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"+iy\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-iy\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(i)(a) Multiply <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(p-4i)/(3-i)\"></span> by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3+i)/(3+i)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>The result is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"[3p+4+(p-12)i]/10\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Multiply by 5, subtract 7 and divide by 3. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w=(3p-10)/6+i(p-12)/6\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) Set the real part to zero: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=10/3\"></span>. The imaginary part is negative, as required. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(ii) Put <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=x+iy\"></span>. The left side is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+1+i(2-y)\"></span> and the right side is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4y+4ix\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Equating parts gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+1=-4y,\\ 2-y=4x\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Substitute <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2-4x\"></span> to obtain <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15x=9\"></span>, hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3/5,\\ y=-2/5\"></span>. Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=(3-2i)/5\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 12 marks.</p>",
